[0011] Embodiments disclosed herein relate to a method for safe mixed-reality visualization of one or mor laser beams. The method may include receiving a plurality of images captured by a plurality of cameras fitted to a headset component. The method may further include combining the plurality of images into a single combined image using a computing device. The computing device may be communicatively coupled with the plurality of cameras and the headset component. The combined image may show one or more laser beams emitted from one or more laser sources in relation to a surrounding environment. The method may further include displaying the combined image to the user via the headset component. The method may additionally include defining the one or more laser beams in the com-bined image, defining a threshold distance from each laser beam, detecting one or more objects within the threshold distance, and transmitting an alert to the display component upon detecting one or more objects within the threshold distance.
[0012] Embodiments disclosed herein relate to a mountable optical device configured to be attached to one or more optical elements. The device may include a mounting component and one or mo inner optical components operatively coupled to the mounting compo-nent. The inner optical components may include an optical fil-tor configured to reduce saturation caused by one or more la-ser beams in the image generated by the camera.",
