title: SYSTEMS AND METHODS FOR MACHINE LEARNING BASED IMAGE PROCESSING
technical_field
[0001] This disclosure relates generally to image processing technologies, and more particularly to systems and methods for employing machine learning models for image processing.
background art
[0002] As technology advances, the use of digital devices has increased significantly. Digital cameras have become ubiquitous and are often used to capture images of documents such as checks, receipts, identification cards, etc. However, these captured images frequently suffer from various issues which prevent them from being suitable for subsequent analysis. For example, poor lighting conditions, low resolution, and movement during capture can cause distortion, blur, glare, and noise in the resulting images. Furthermore, the images may not be properly aligned (e.g., skewed) making it difficult to accurately extract information from the images. These problems can result in errors in downstream processes where the images are analyzed for information extraction, validation, fraud detection, and authentication purposes.
summary of invention
[0003] Systems and methods described herein relate to image processing using machine learning models. In some embodiments, an apparatus may comprise a processor configured to obtain image data depicting a document from a user device. The processor may generate a bounding box indicating a set of boundaries between a document and a background in the image data, based upon pixel data of the image data corresponding to the bounding box. The processor may also generate a dynamic alignment indicator comprising a visual element indicating the bounding box for display at a user interface of the user-device. Additionally, the processor may generate an image quality score for the image data based on a distance of a feature vector for the document and one or more stored feature vectors. Each stored feature vector represents one or more reference features of a reference document. When the image quality score does not satisfy an image quality threshold, the processor may generate an adjustment prompt for display at the user interface of the device, prompting the user to reposition their device relative to the document. [0004] According to certain aspects, the processor may receive a video feed comprising multiple frames from the user device, detect the document in the image data of at least a single frame of the video feed, and select one or more frames of a plurality of frames having the image data that satisfies a quality selection threshold for the document. [0005] Further, the processor may execute an object recognition engine of a machine-learning architecture that uses a video feed as an input, the object recognition model trained for detecting a type of document in the video feed. Alternatively or additionally, the processor may execute an object recognition engine that detects content data of the document in the image data. [0006] Moreover, the processor may generate an output image representing the document for display at a user interface of the user's device. Additionally or alternatively, the processor may generate a confirmation prompt for display at the user interface, the confirmation prompt including the content data extracted form the document. The processor may then receive a confirmation input from the user device indicating confirmation or rejection of the content data extracted from the document. [0007] In addition, the processor may generate a risk score for the document based on a distance of the feature vector of the document and one or both of a stored feature vector representing one or more reference features and/or a predefined template. If the risk score exceeds a risk threshold, the processor may flag the document for review by a human operator. [0008] In accordance with certain aspects, the processor may update the bounding box indication of the set of boundaries between the document and the background in the image data, based upon pixel values of the image data corresponding to the document. The processor may also generate a second label annotation for the image data, corresponding to the bounding box. [0009] Yet further, the processor may generate an augmented image overlay for the image data, including the dynamic alignment indicator over the document in image data, the augmented image overlay including a visual element corresponding to at least one of a corner, an edge, or a data field of the document. [0010] Another embodiment provides a system comprising a memory storing instructions executable by a processor to perform actions comprising: obtaining image data depicting a document from a user device; generating a bounding box indicating a set of boundaries between document and a background in the image data, using pixel data of the image data corresponding to the bounds of the document; generating a dynamic alignment indicator comprising a visual element indicating positioning for the document overlaid for display at a UI of the user device based upon the bounding box; extracting a feature vector for the 