  "summary_of_invention": "[0005] Embodiments of the present disclosure aim to solve at least one or all of the above problems existing in related art. One aspect of the present disclosure provides a method for motion prediction. The method can be applied to a scenario where multiple targets move simultaneously, and the method can predict the future positions of these targets through machine learning algorithms and control the camera accordingly. The embodiments of the present disclosure improve the accuracy of the predicted position of each target through multi-target fusion, thereby improving the quality of the final image.
[0006] According to an embodiment of the present disclosure, a method for motion prediction is provided. The method comprises:
[0007] receiving spatial information output by a radio-wave sensor,
[0008] wherein the spatial information comprises position and velocity of a plurality of points;
[0009] receiving an image captured by a camera;
[0010] tracking a plurality of objects based on the spatial information and the image to acquire a consolidated tracking result;
[0011] predicting a motion trajectory of the plurality of objects based on the consolidated tracking result to acquire a prediction result; and
[0012] controlling the camera according to the prediction result.
[0013] In some embodiments, the step of tracking a plurality of objects based on the spatial inforn- mation and the image to acquire a consolidated tracking result comprises:
[0014] determining whether a first object among the plurality of objects has a high speed based on the spatial information;
[0015] if the first object does not have a high speed, determining a second object among the plurality of objects corresponding to the first object based on the spatial information;
[0016] performing feature extraction from the second object based on the spatial information;
[0077] performing feature matching between the first object and the second object based on the extracted features;
[0018] obtaining the consolidated tracking result based on the feature match-ing result.
[0019] In some embodiments, the step of performing feature ex- traction from the second object based on the spatial informa-tion comprises:
[0020] extracting a contour feature of the second object based on the spatial information;
s [0021] extracting a color feature of the second object based on the spatial infonnation; and
[0022] combining the contour feature and the color feature into a single feature vector.
[0023] In some embodiments, the step of performing fea-ture matching between the first object and the second object com-prises:
[0024] calculating a distance between the first object and the sec-ond object based on the combined feature vector;
[0025] comparing the calculated distance with a threshold value;
[0026] if the calculated distance is less than the threshold value, deter-mining that the first object corresponds to the second object;
[0027] otherwise, determining that the first object does not cor-respond to the second object.
[0028] In some embodiments, the step of predicting a motion trajectory of the plurality of objects comprises:
[0029] training a neural network model using historical data corre-sponding to a plurality of frames;
[0030] inputting current data corresponding to the plurality of frames into the trained neural network model to determine a pre-diction result of the plurality of objects.
[0031] In some embodiments, the step of training the neu-ral network model using historical data corresponding to a plu-rality of frames comprises:
[0032] dividing the historical data into a training set and a vali-dation set;
[0033] generating a loss function based on the training set;
[0034] updating parameters of the neural network model based on the generated loss function; and
[0035] evaluating performance of the updated neural network mod-el based on the validation set.
[0036] In some embodiments, the step of updating param-eters of the neural network model based on the generated losss function comprises:
[0037] backpropagating errors of the generated loss function to adjust the parameters of the neural network model.
[0038] In some embodiments, the step of evaluating per-formance of the updated neural network model based on the validation set comprises:
[0039] determining a mean absolute error (MAE) between actual values and predicted values obtained after running the updated neural network model on the validation set;
[0040] determining a root mean squared percentage error (RMSPE) between the actual values and the predicted values obtained after running the updated neural network mod-el on the validation set; and
determining a coefficient of determination (R-squared) between the actual values and the predicted values ob-tained after running the updated neural network model on the valuation set.
[0041] In some embodiments, the step of inputting cur-rent data corresponding to the plurality of frames into the train-ed neural network model to determine a prediction result of the plurality of objects comprises:
[0042] normalizing the current data before inputting them into the trained neural network model;
[0043] denormalizing the normalized current data after they are processed by the trained neural network model.
[0044] In some embodiments, the step of normalizing the current data before inputting them comprises:
[0045] subtracting a minimum value of the current data from the current data to get a difference value;
[0046] dividing the difference value by a range of the current data.
[0047] In some embodiments, the step of denormaliz-ing the normalized current data after they are processed by
the trained neural network model comprises:
[0048] multiplying the normalized current data by a range of the current data;
[0049] adding the multiplied normalized current data by the min-imum value of the current data.
[0050] In some embodiments, the step of controlling the cam-era according to the prediction result comprises:
[0051] adjusting a focus of the camera according to the predic-tion result;
[0052] adjusting a zoom ratio of the camera according to the predication result;
[0053] adjusting a pan angle of the camera according to the pre-diction result;
[0054] adjusting a tilt angle of the camera according to the predi-cition result;
[0055] adjusting a roll angle of the camera according to the pre-dictlon result; or
[0056] adjusting a direction of the camera according to the pre-diction re sult.
[0057] Another aspect of the present disclosure provides an elec-tronic device for motion prediction. The electronic device is configured to implement any of the methods described above.
[0058] It should be noted that the aforementioned embodi-ments are merely examples, rather than limitative, and those skilled in the art will understand that many modifications and variations can be made without departing from the scope of protection defined by the appended claims.",
